Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Automated theorem provers (non",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["-", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "32d5a1e8-6773-4655-b24e-eb5f10c3f81c"],
 "AI)"
}], "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.965020288869409*^9, 
  3.965020298133449*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ce7519e4-c4e3-4139-978e-\
804502601a93"],

Cell["\<\
Classical systems like E-prover, Vampire, Prover9, and SMT solvers like Z3, \
CVC5 already solve many algebraic problems (equalities, ring reasoning, etc.) \
\[LongDash] but they are not \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]AI\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], they\[CloseCurlyQuote]re \
highly engineered search systems.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.965020302374899*^9},ExpressionUUID->"c5a0e497-4be0-4a63-a665-\
e8ea5a1e0857"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "These can sometimes generate proof objects, but usually not in the \
narrative style of algebra proofs. Maybe a well",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["-", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "ce2ba509-2969-4b6e-b310-ac2355451ae9"],
 "documented github page or something?undedibality...concept of \
undecidbaility to prove that stuff and it might be worth the effort. And then \
I can try to prove something in that area. And that machine learning \
causality does seem very interesting. Hmm. I don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t know now. \
It is confusing. I don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t know whether i want to edit that \
paper or not. Seems like I won\[CloseCurlyQuote]t ahve time. I don\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]t know. Interesting. Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s see."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.965020305107758*^9, 3.965020323661203*^9}, {
  3.965304154683494*^9, 3.9653041656223793`*^9}, {3.965304442649105*^9, 
