Cell[TextData[{
 "Hmm. I don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t completely get this algorithm. This is \
basically reinforcement learning. In every iteration we generate a large \
number of random sessions (constructions) following the above method. We \
calculate the reward for each, and throw away all but the top",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{" ", "y"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "aa56b047-b4bc-4795-ae6e-0f27b1dcea9f"],
 " percentile. The the network learns form the remaiing sessions, where the \
neural network adjusts weights so that it outputs the best possible \
construction. This is called reinforcement. Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s learn this."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.963984912419935*^9, 3.963984913748113*^9}, {
  3.963984970146617*^9, 3.963984982972423*^9}, {3.963985021208906*^9, 
  3.963985040688803*^9}, {3.963985906401916*^9, 3.96398597866696*^9}, {
  3.963986014072893*^9, 
  3.963986017356674*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b691794b-f268-4a00-afea-\
6735607553ce"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Closed]],

